// `Instruction.ChangeLife` under Lean's own name for it: the alias
// `declare_semantic_primitives` generates, so a card writes a macro where the
// basis has a constructor (ADR 12.1). Unlike the other aliases it keeps its
// agent: extort's "each opponent loses 1 life and you gain life equal to the
// total life lost this way" is refused when the loss is handed to each
// opponent (Lean `quantOutcomeInScope 0`), so it writes the group as the
// agent here.
(
    name: "changeLife",
    kinds: [Instruction],
    params: {"delta": Delta, "agent": Subject},
    body: ChangeLife(delta: Param(delta), agent: Param(agent)),
)
